.TH SDL_FALLTHROUGH 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_FALLTHROUGH \- A macro to signal that a case statement without a
.BR break
is intentional.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_begin_code.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_FALLTHROUGH [[fallthrough]]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
C compilers have gotten more aggressive about warning when a switch\(aqs
.BR case
block does not end with a
.BR break
or other flow control statement, flowing into the next case\(aqs code, as this is a common accident that leads to strange bugs\[char46] But sometimes falling through to the next case is the correct and desired behavior\[char46] This symbol lets an app communicate this intention to the compiler, so it doesn\(aqt generate a warning\[char46]
.PP
It is used like this:

.IP
.EX
switch (x) {
    case 1:
        DoSomethingOnlyForOne();
        SDL_FALLTHROUGH;  // tell the compiler this was intentional.
    case 2:
        DoSomethingForOneAndTwo();
        break;
}
.EE
.PP

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

